r": 2025, "rank": 376, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 108, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 81, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 352, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500--retailing", "title": "Fortune Sector Leaders: Retailing", "year": 2024, "rank": 8, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 100, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 311, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 35, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 94, "itemDescription": "The electronics retailer with more than 900 stores nationwide struggled through a difficult year, falling 26 spots on this year\u2019s Fortune 500 list.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>Revenue fell 11% to $46 billion and profit fell 42% to $1.4 billion.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The company is predicting that customers will soon repair or upgrade all the home devices they bought during the pandemic, leading to an uptick in revenue.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>Best Buy laid off hundreds of in-store employees in April 2023 in what the company called a rethinking of its retail experience as more shopping moves online.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The company had 90,000 workers in the U.S. and Canada as of January 2023, down from nearly 125,000 workers in early 2020.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>CEO Corie Barry is one of 52 female CEOs leading Fortune 500 companies.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 258, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "modern-board-25", "title": "Fortune Modern Board 25", "year": 2022, "rank": 21, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Best Buy\u2019s board includes three former CEOs and four active CEOs, including its own chief, Corie Barry, as well as David Kenny (Nielsen), Steve Rendle (VF Corp.), and Eugene Woods (Atrium Health). Best Buy scored high on board size, its CEO succession plan, and senior independent nonexecutive director representation.</span><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Other notable names among its directors include Karen McLoughlin, former CFO of Cognizant Technology Solutions, and Mario Marte, current CFO of Chewy.\u00a0</span><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Best Buy reported sales of $51.7 billion in the fiscal year ended January 2022, registering double-digit sales growth even as it grappled with the COVID pandemic, inflation, and supply-chain shortages.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 68, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Best Buy was able to post record-high revenues and earnings in 2021, though the road ahead for the consumer electronics retailer isn\u2019t necessarily smooth. Fourth-quarter 2021 sales declined year over year in the U.S. as supply-chain issues and the continuing decline in popularity of in-person shopping dogged the company. More than 20 brick-and-mortar Best Buy stores closed last year, and more are expected to shut down in 2022. Still, Best Buy has had success in expanding its e-commerce and online shopping offerings; nearly 40% of the company\u2019s domestic revenue now comes from e-commerce.\u00a0</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 238, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;As screen time soared in 2020, so did Best Buy. Revenue at the electronics retailer rose 8.3% to $47 billion in 2020 compared with the prior year\u2014enough to push the company up nine spots on the Fortune 500 list this year. Profit, meanwhile, climbed a hefty 16.7%. The good news came, in part, from the work-from-home revolution, as newly remote workers stocked up on home office equipment and other technology. But it's not rosy for everyone at Best Buy. The retailer expects online shopping to account for 40% of sales next year compared to just 19% two years earlier\u2014which prompted the company to announce store closures and 5,000 layoffs in early 2021. &quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\">As screen time soared in 2020, so did Best Buy. Revenue at the electronics retailer rose 8.3% to $47 billion in 2020 compared with the prior year\u2014enough to push the company up 37 spots on the Global 500 list this year. Profit, meanwhile, climbed a hefty 16.7%. The good news came, in part, from the work-from-home revolution, as newly remote workers stocked up on home office equipment and other technology. But it's not rosy for everyone at Best Buy. The retailer expects online shopping to account for 40% of sales next year compared to just 19% two years earlier\u2014which prompted the company to announce store closures and 5,000 layoffs in early 2021. </span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 66, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;As screen time soared in 2020, so did Best Buy. Revenue at the electronics retailer rose 8.3% to $47 billion in 2020 compared with the prior year\u2014enough to push the company up nine spots on the Fortune 500 list this year. Profit, meanwhile, climbed a hefty 16.7%. The good news came, in part, from the work-from-home revolution, as newly remote workers stocked up on home office equipment and other technology. But it's not rosy for everyone at Best Buy. The retailer expects online shopping to account for 40% of sales next year compared to just 19% two years earlier\u2014which prompted the company to announce store closures and 5,000 layoffs in early 2021. &quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\">As screen time soared in 2020, so did Best Buy. Revenue at the electronics retailer rose 8.3% to $47 billion in 2020 compared with the prior year\u2014enough to push the company up nine spots on the Fortune 500 list this year. Profit, meanwhile, climbed a hefty 16.7%. The good news came, in part, from the work-from-home revolution, as newly remote workers stocked up on home office equipment and other technology. But it's not rosy for everyone at Best Buy. The retailer expects online shopping to account for 40% of sales next year compared to just 19% two years earlier\u2014which prompted the company to announce store closures and 5,000 layoffs in early 2021. </span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 275, "itemDescription": "Corie Barry, who became CEO of the retailer in June 2019, oversaw a rise in online sales during her first year in the job: Digital orders accounted for nearly 20% of the company\u2019s $43.6 billion in revenue last year. But after frenetic consumer demand in March\u2014as the newly self-isolated stocked up on laptops, refrigerators, and devices that could be used for remote learning\u2014Best Buy, like most retailers, began feeling the sting of the pandemic. The 54-year-old chain in April furloughed 51,000 of its 125,000 employees, including nearly all part-time workers."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 75, "itemDescription": "Corie Barry, who became CEO of the retailer in June 2019, oversaw a rise in online sales during her first year in the job: Digital orders accounted for nearly 20% of the company\u2019s $43.6 billion in revenue last year. But after frenetic consumer demand in March\u2014as the newly self-isolated stocked up on laptops, refrigerators, and devices that could be used for remote learning\u2014Best Buy, like most retailers, began feeling the sting of the pandemic. The 54-year-old chain in April furloughed 51,000 of its 125,000 employees, including nearly all part-time workers."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 276, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 74, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2019, "rank": 32, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 261, "itemDescription": 